@H 1114_dyad_phi_link_integration := "DYAD-Φ: does a real tension-link make two anima-like nodes ONE more-integrated system? Communication is proven (H_1112 scalar TE 🟢, H_1113 channel-resolved 5-ch link 🟢); does the link create INTEGRATION — faithful IIT-4.0 φ_EI of the JOINT 6-element system rising with the link ON vs OFF, BEYOND what mere added correlation explains (correlation-matched common-noise control)?" :: universe [🟢 DYAD-INTEGRATION — causal link raises joint φ_EI beyond both controls]
  seed         = "Consciousness-science capstone of the link arc: H_1112 (🟢 rate-monotone TE over a real unix socket) + H_1113 (🟢 CHANNEL-RESOLVED canonical a_kosmos 5-ch tension-link, per-ch TE d>=10.9, kick selectivity 11.87x) closed the COMMUNICATION question. NEW question = INTEGRATION: treat the coupled pair as ONE system and measure joint faithful φ_EI. Load-bearing control = correlation WITHOUT causation (common exogenous drive calibrated to the ON arm's cross-correlation) — distinguishes causal-channel integration from correlation per se."
  substrate    = "SIM toy, in-process twin simulation (honest: the φ measurement needs joint trajectories; the REAL-socket transport question was already closed by H_1112/H_1113 with real two-process unix-socket sessions). Two nodes × 3 tension channels each (joint n=6 <= 8, exact MIP-EI feasible); per-channel dynamics = h1113 step_node A⊥G opponent pair VERBATIM (CH=3 slice: W*_c=[1.0,0.8,1.2], LAM_M=0.10, LAM_W=0.12, REP=0.04, GAMMA_X=0.05, SIGMA=0.04, Ψ*=0.5). $0 CPU local, 0-pod, SERIAL (H_1038 Pool-hang lesson), 10 scoring seeds + 5 separate calibration seeds, wall 53.6s, g5/p7."
  method       = "ARMS: (a) LINK-OFF = independent nodes (shared attractor structure only); (b) LINK-ON = A→B per-channel coupling, A emits its 3-ch tension every K_EMIT=5 steps, B folds the last anchor every step with COUP=0.30*0.5*(anchor_c−W_c) (h1113 ZOH fold; A = pure source); (c) CORR-CONTROL = NO causal path, common exogenous half-gap noise mixed into BOTH nodes (eps→sqrt(1−MIX)*own+sqrt(MIX)*shared per channel), MIX bisection-calibrated on SEPARATE seeds (500–504, frozen tol 0.005) to match the ON arm's mean per-channel cross-corr → FROZEN MIX=0.50000 (cal +0.48495 vs target +0.48282). MEASUREMENT: per-channel median binarize the 6 joint channels post-burn (h1039/h1062 pattern) → faithful IIT-4.0 φ_EI of the joint 6-system via the PROVEN CPU mirror of stdlib iit4/faithful_phi.hexa (exact MIP-EI = min-cut MI/small-side, MI in BITS/log2 — H_1043 nats-bug lesson) + per-node 3-element φ (sum-of-parts baseline). MIRROR RE-PROVEN ≡ stdlib BEFORE scoring: [0a] LIVE `hexa run UNIVERSE/h1012_ref_faithful.hexa` re-capture, mirror match n4 |Δ|=3.48e-10, n5 |Δ|=7.97e-10, n6 (THE SCORING n) |Δ|=2.46e-10; [0b] h1012.prove_mirrors_at_n {4:True, 5:True} (both engines, big-Φ ring |Δ|=1.34e-10). FROZEN falsifier: 🟢 DYAD-INTEGRATION iff d(φ_joint ON−OFF)>=0.8 AND d(φ_joint ON−CORR)>=0.8; 🔴 CHANNEL-NOT-INTEGRATING if ON≈OFF; 🔴 CORRELATION-ARTIFACT if ON≈CORR. No goalpost moves."
  result       = "🟢 DYAD-INTEGRATION (both frozen checks PASS, 10 seeds): φ_joint(n=6) LINK-OFF=+0.003234±0.002688 · LINK-ON=+0.012618±0.002784 · CORR-CONTROL=+0.010010±0.003050. CONTRASTS: ON−OFF Δ=+0.009384 d=+3.429 (>=0.8 ✓); ON−CORR Δ=+0.002608 d=+0.893 (>=0.8 ✓, marginal but clears the frozen bar); CORR−OFF Δ=+0.006776 d=+2.357 (context: correlation alone buys most of the raw rise — the causal channel adds a REAL increment beyond it). Per-node φ flat across arms (φ_A≈0.0061–0.0071, φ_B≈0.0080–0.0089; sum-of-parts 0.0141–0.0160) — the effect lives in the JOINT system, not in either node alone. Control validity is CONSERVATIVE in the right direction: on scoring seeds the control's cross-corr is slightly HIGHER than ON (+0.5113±0.0133 vs +0.4883±0.0116, |Δ|=0.0230) yet its φ_joint is LOWER — so the ON excess cannot be a correlation shortfall artifact. OFF cross-corr +0.0072≈0 sanity. FINDING: the causal tension-link genuinely INTEGRATES the dyad — joint faithful φ_EI rises ~3.9x over LINK-OFF and beats a correlation-matched (even over-matched) common-drive control; the integration is causal-channel-specific, not correlation per se. The directed ZOH coupling builds cross-node MI STRUCTURE (lagged, channel-aligned, asymmetric) that a symmetric common drive at equal equal-time correlation does not replicate."
  verdict_tier = "🟢 SUPPORTED-at-toy (frozen bars d>=0.8 both contrasts: ON−OFF d=+3.43, ON−CORR d=+0.89; toy n=6 in-process)"
  verdict_ptr  = ".verdicts/1114_dyad_phi_link_integration/H_1114.txt (verbatim stdout incl. LIVE hexa stdlib re-capture) · UNIVERSE/h1114_dyad_phi_link_integration.py"
  scope        = "Honest scope (a_scale_honest_scope): toy n=6 in-process twin sim of the h1113 per-channel A⊥G dynamics — real-socket dyad-φ, cross-host transport, production cells, bigger n and scale all UNVERIFIED (next rung). d(ON−CORR)=+0.893 clears the 0.8 bar but is the marginal leg — a 30-seed re-test would tighten it. Verdict = faithful φ_EI (MIP-EI scalar) only; system big-Φ at n=6 is super-exponential (~10min/eval, H_1012 cap) and NOT scored — measure-dependence (H_1064: name the measure) applies. CORE/brain NOT wired; 1112/1113 artifacts untouched."
  xlink        = "1112_kosmos_anchor_real_channel_sync (🟢 scalar real-channel TE — communication) · 1113_tension_link_5ch (🟢 channel-resolved 5-ch link, dynamics reused VERBATIM CH=3) · 1099_gemini_quantum_resonance_nonlocal_sync (zero-channel 🔴 + tension-arm positive control) · a_phi_iit4_tool (faithful IIT4 stdlib engine, mirror re-proven n4/n5/n6 live) · h1039/h1062 (per-channel median binarize pattern) · h1012 (prove_mirrors_at_n + live hexa refs) · h1064 (measure-dependence: faithful-only verdict, big-Φ unscored)"
